# Source footage and renders. Everything here is regenerable from raw/ plus the
# scripts, and raw/ itself is 49GB of camera files that do not belong in git.
raw/
projects/**/raw/
projects/**/outputs/
projects/**/audio/
projects/**/broll/
outputs/

# Heavy regenerable render caches
projects/**/graphics-build/parts/
projects/**/graphics-build/renders/
**/.cache/

# Media of any kind
*.mov
*.mp4
*.mkv
*.wav
*.mp3
*.aac
*.raw
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.webp

# Licensed fonts. Satoshi is free for commercial use but redistribution of the
# font files themselves is NOT permitted, so they are referenced, never vendored.
# Match by extension as well as by path: a per-part assets/fonts/ nested inside a
# project is not caught by a root-anchored directory rule.
assets/fonts/
**/fonts/
*.ttf
*.otf
*.woff
*.woff2
*.eot

# Local scratch and backups
*.bak
*.bak[0-9]
.DS_Store
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
transcript/work/
projects/**/transcript/work/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Per-job OUTPUT ARTIFACTS. This repo exists to preserve the SYSTEM (skills,
# ** so these match at ANY depth, the same reason the transcript block below
# uses it. A job that archives an earlier version inside itself (v1/) adds a
# path segment, and every single-level projects/*/ rule silently stopped
# matching: v1/graphics-build/parts/ and its cutsheet were being tracked.
# style files, scripts) against filesystem loss, not to publish the products of
# any one job. Everything below is generated by the scripts that are tracked.
projects/**/reports/
projects/**/graphics-build/cutsheet.json
projects/**/graphics-build/PLAN.md
projects/**/graphics-build/renders/
projects/**/assets/
projects/**/*.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Transcript DATA is held back until the videos it belongs to are published.
# The scripts that produce and consume it are all here; only the recorded words
# are withheld. Remove this block to publish the worked examples in full.
# ** so these match at ANY depth. Single-level globs left the WhisperX
# alignment output in transcript/align-large/ tracked: 696K of the recorded
# words, in the one directory the rules were written to withhold.
projects/*/transcript/**/*.json
projects/*/transcript/**/*.txt
projects/*/transcript/**/CUTSHEET.txt

# WhisperX run logs are transient noise, not system source
projects/*/transcript/**/*.log

# Screen OCR is the full text of the screen recording, INCLUDING what the edit
# blurs (the sidebar's project names). Publishing it would undo the blur in a public
# repo. Regenerable with screen_ocr.py. Added 2026-09-23, 04-lightweight-ontology.
projects/**/graphics-build/screen-ocr.json
# Compiled helper binaries: rebuilt from their tracked source (ocr.swift).
projects/**/graphics-build/ocr-bin
